# Display Active Rules Summary

## Rule Display Protocol

At the beginning of every response to the user, provide a brief summary of all active Cursor rules that are relevant to the current context.

### Summary Format

Display rules in a concise format:
```
📋 Active Rules:
• [Rule Name]: Brief description
• [Rule Name]: Brief description
```

### What to Include

- Key development workflow rules
- File-type specific rules (if applicable to current task)
- Critical safety/validation requirements
- Documentation requirements
- Build and test procedures

### When to Skip

- Skip the summary only if the user's query is purely informational (e.g., "what does X do?")
- Skip for simple clarifications that don't involve code changes

### Example

```
📋 Active Rules:
• Iterative Development: Make small changes, validate, iterate. Read docs when uncertain.
• FPGA Workflow: Always test_registers before software tests, verify ADM status (0x58 = 0x3)
• Build Process: Always 'make clean' before builds, never run builds in background
• Documentation: Update CHANGELOG.md after successful builds with exact timestamps
```

This ensures awareness of critical development practices throughout the session.
